# Doggywood visual change control

Visual design is product-owner controlled.

Do not change a visual element unless the current instruction explicitly names it, or the change is absolutely required to make requested functionality work.

## Frozen

Never modify without explicit product-owner instruction: header, desktop hero, mobile hero, trust strip, logos, and brand assets.

## Approved section backgrounds

Below the trust strip, alternate only:

- `#FFFFFF`
- `#FFF9E2`

Sequence: About `#FFFFFF` → How It Works `#FFF9E2` → How Voting Works `#FFFFFF` → Enter `#FFF9E2` → Contest Rules `#FFFFFF` → FAQ `#FFF9E2` → Final CTA `#FFFFFF` → Footer `#FFFFFF`.

Do not introduce new background colors. Gold is an accent (buttons, icons, small labels), not an unapproved full-width section background.

## Scope

Backend, auth, email, SMS, database, sessions, APIs, and security work must not modify styling, colors, typography, layout, imagery, or responsive behavior.

Do not treat “clean it up”, “make it better”, “implement the feature”, or “refactor” as permission to redesign.
